# Citation metadata for the hazrisk software (https://citation-file-format.github.io).
# GitHub's "Cite this repository" button and Zenodo read this file.
# At release: fill in `version` and `date-released`; after the first release,
# add the Zenodo concept DOI as `doi`.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "hazrisk: seismic hazard-curve approximation and risk integration"
abstract: >-
  hazrisk is a Python library for seismic risk calculations from a hazard
  curve and a fragility curve. It fits first-order (power law) and
  second-order (log-quadratic) approximations to numerical hazard curves,
  evaluates the SAC/FEMA closed-form solutions for the mean annual frequency
  of a limit state and the median capacity required for a target frequency,
  integrates lognormal fragility curves numerically against tabulated hazard
  curves with PCHIP interpolation, and computes the contribution of each
  intensity level to the risk.
